course: dictionary
lesson: 15679
title: An old word: tidings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tidings means news, especially important news. It is an old-fashioned word, and you will almost always see it in its plural form, tidings, even when it is one piece of news. Today people more often say news or word.
explain: Context gives you clues. «The messenger rode into the village with tidings of the king's wedding.» A messenger carries a message, and a royal wedding is big news, so tidings must mean news. Check it by swapping: «with news of the king's wedding» still makes sense.
explain: You will often meet «good tidings» in old Christmas songs and in the Bible. Good tidings means good news. In the Bible, an angel brings «good tidings of great joy» to the shepherds, so the shepherds hear wonderful news.
fact: Tidings means news or information, especially important news.
fact: Tidings is an old-fashioned word, and it is usually used in its plural form.
fact: «Good tidings» means good news.
fact: You will find «good tidings» in Christmas carols, such as «Good tidings we bring to you and your kin».
fact: Clues like a messenger or a wedding can help you work out what tidings means.
exercise: «The messenger rode in with tidings of the king's wedding.» What does tidings mean here? | Dancing | *News | Weather reports | Sleep
exercise: In an old carol, the singers bring «good tidings». What does good tidings mean? | Good weather | Good luck charms | *Good news | Good food
exercise: Find the word that means about the same as tidings. | Songs | Riddles | Stories | *News
test: «Ruby read the tidings in the letter: her cousin was coming to stay.» What does tidings mean? | Pictures | *News | Puzzles | Jokes
test: The Bible says an angel brought good tidings of great joy to the shepherds. What does this tell us? | The shepherds were sad | The shepherds were cold | *The shepherds heard good news | The shepherds were lost
exam: Which swap keeps the meaning of tidings in «Old tidings travelled slowly by horse»? | *Old news | Old trees | Old boots | Old songs
